# Golgari Grave-Troll: "If you return Golgari Grave-Troll from your graveyard directly to the battlefield, its first ability
# counts itself" (its ruling; CR 614.12): the counters are counted as it would enter, while it is still in the graveyard.
# Reanimate brings it back from a graveyard where it is the only creature card: one +1/+1 counter, a 1/1 (counted from
# elsewhere it would be a 0/0, put into the graveyard at once). Bot1 loses 2 life to Thoughtseize and 5, the Troll's mana
# value, to Reanimate.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Thoughtseize
Mox Jet
Reanimate
Golgari Grave-Troll
Plains
Plains
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thoughtseize.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Choose(Golgari Grave-Troll)
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Reanimate.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Golgari Grave-Troll)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Golgari Grave-Troll.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Golgari Grave-Troll.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Golgari Grave-Troll.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Reanimate; Thoughtseize
Bot1.Life = 13
